text:
- Test-only binaries, never in a release build: `viola-fake-agent` (a `[[bin]]` of the root package behind feature `fake-agent`, the stand-in `claude`; its print mode `-p <prompt>` / `--print <prompt>` writes its start receipts, fires the SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit (prompt set), Stop and SessionEnd `default` fixtures, prints `ok` on stdout and exits 0, never raw and never reading stdin — the mode `viola verify`'s print probe drives in CI; thirteen argv options (the count's rule is this list), no env, of which nine serve verify's interactive runs and their tests: `--trusted-root <DIR>` (an ancestor walk, both paths canonicalised), `--screens` (writes `Screen.modal` when untrusted, no hook fired, or `Screen.ready` when trusted, SessionStart as before: a clear, then rows joined by CRLF), `--turn-stop` (a submit fires UserPromptSubmit, then Stop, then writes `Screen.turn`), `--dialogs` (a pasted compiled dialog prompt replays its recorded `<stem>-<n>` variants in claim order: a call's PreToolUse fires first; with no decision, its PermissionRequest fires; a decision from either fires its PostToolUse), `--framing` (a pasted compiled paste text fires its recorded `paste-1` / `paste-2` / `paste-3` UserPromptSubmit variant with its bytes unchanged, a new stem reached through `ledger::framing_stem` with no option added, the probed local command fires the recorded `clear-1` SessionEnd then SessionStart and no UserPromptSubmit, and `/compact` fires the recorded `SessionStart.compact-1` with `session_id` set to the last SessionStart the agent fired (the launch one or a replayed clear's; only a SessionStart whose fixture exists moves it) and no UserPromptSubmit;
 a set without a variant fires nothing for it) and the two test-only holds `--stop-receipt-hold-ms <n>` (capped at 1 000 ms, a hold of the Stop hook's receipt that forces a race window open) and `--paste-hint-ms <ms>` (capped at 10 000 ms; with `--framing`, after the long text's replay and its Stop the screen is cleared and `Screen.turn` is drawn only after the hold), and the test-only screen switch `--tag-turn-screen <phase>` (with `--framing` and `--turn-stop`: after the turn of the compiled tag-like paste, and after no other turn, `Screen.<phase>` of the set is drawn in place of `Screen.turn`; a missing file draws nothing), and the test-only screen switch `--long-turn-screen <phase>` (with `--framing` and `--turn-stop`: after the long paste's turn alone, after its Stop, `Screen.<phase>` of the set is drawn in place of `Screen.turn`), and two serve `viola revive`'s tests and, under the fake agent, verify's Run E: `--resume <id>` (the SessionStart fired at launch is the set's recorded `SessionStart.resume-1.json` when the set holds it (`RESUME_VARIANT`, `launch_variant`; 2.1.287 since chunk 2026-10-14-resume-and-compact-ledger-rows), else its recorded `SessionStart.default` payload, with `source` set to `resume` and `session_id` set to the id given, the trailing newline kept) and `--fork-session` (beside `--resume`, `session_id` is the compiled id `0f0e0d0c-0b0a-4908-8706-050403020100`; alone it changes nothing); without `--resume` every payload is the recorded bytes; and two serve the statusline tests: `--settings <file>` and `--statusline-stdin <file>` (with both, and only when the settings file's `statusLine` command, split on ASCII white space, is an absolute command, it runs that command with the stdin file's bytes and files a `statusline` receipt, the `hook` receipt's fields without `event`);
 `--framing` with `--settings <file>` alone replays the set's recorded status line the same way, the one word exactly `"$0"` handed over as `/bin/sh`, spawned directly and never through a shell: `StatusLine.default-1.json` after the launch SessionStart's hooks and `StatusLine.rate-limits-1.json` once at the end of the first Stop's turn, after the turn screen (a relative command is receipted and never run; a set without the variants fires nothing; no option added); beside the options it takes two mode words: `statusline-echo`, which prints its output and files its stdin and exits with the code after the marker path, and `agents` (chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board), which answers `agents --json` from files beside its own executable: `agents-mode` (`recorded` · `oversize` · `malformed`, absent read as `recorded`), `agents-rows.json` (planted rows, printed unchanged) and a live `sessions/<pid>.json` registry its interactive runs write (a row written just before its launch SessionStart fires, its `cwd` the launch fixture's recorded `cwd`, `~` without one; a dead or reused pid left out through one `viola_state::liveness::start_times()` read); no option and no env are added (the founder's own answer to P4 fork 2, that chunk's `inputs#I1`)) and `viola-harness` (in `viola-e2e`, behind `scripts/agent-run.{sh,ps1}`; its command contract is test-plan §3) and `viola-mcp-tap` (a `[[bin]]` of `viola-e2e` that records a live MCP exchange for the `Mcp.` fixtures, Repository below: `record <capture> <viola exe> <args…>` is a direct spawn, no shell and no PATH lookup, each line read through `take(MAX_FRAME)` and appended once, tagged with its direction, to a capture created 0600, exiting with the child;
 `fixture <capture> <out>` keeps the client frames up to and including the first `tools/list` request and each request's result keyed by method, through `ledger::scrub` (the home → `~`, the user word → `<user>`) and then `ledger::screen_fault` over every string and key, refusing with the file name and one closed code `home-path` · `absolute-path` · `username` · `email`, never the content).

- `diagnostics/`: home-level per-role process logs, codes only: `run-<name>.ndjson`, `hook-<name>.ndjson`, `mcp.ndjson` and `cli-<name>.ndjson`.
 `run` (and `viola revive`'s start arm, which logs as process `run` into `run-<name>.ndjson` with `run`'s detail sink once its strict-modes check has passed; `run`'s start and `revive`'s start arm also run the home-tree check through `checked_exe` / `refuse_tree` before `open_wrapper_log`; a refused check, on either `revive` arm or `run`'s start, opens no process log and writes no line), `hook` and the `cli` verbs `verify`, `send`, `wait`, `last`, `list`, `answer`, `pause`, `release`, `link`, `unlink`, `revive --list` and `plugin install` have producers today (`cli-<name>.ndjson`: `send` / `wait` / `last` / `answer` / `pause` / `release` / `link` / `unlink` — `<name>` the target instance, the driven one for `link` / `unlink` — write `process-start`, the client `channel-request` / `channel-response` lines (`wait`'s carry `after` / `timeout_ms` / `outcome`) and `process-exit{subject:"self"}`, exit 21 with `detail:"instance-dead"` + `during`, or `detail:"server-verify-failed"` + `during:"connect"` when the serving process is not the recorded wrapper (then no `channel-request` line), at WARN, with no pid, start time, path or endpoint, exit 20 with `detail:"wrapper-fault"`; a refused instance check of `send`, `wait`, `last`, `answer`, `pause`, `release`, `link` or `unlink` (`client::refuse_untrusted`) opens no role file and writes no line; `list`, only under a parsed `VIOLA_NAME` once its scan passed, one `agents-probe` `process-start` / `process-exit` pair per `claude agents --json` read and one `parse-rejected{parser:"claude-agents-json"}` on an oversize or malformed answer (no row text, id, `cwd` or path; chunk 2026-10-16-unwrapped-sessions-on-the-board), and `viola revive`'s start arm writes its `session-live` reading's `agents-probe` pair into `run-<name>.ndjson` and, on a `session-live` refusal, one `process-exit{subject:"self", exit_code:1, detail:"session-live"}`; `viola revive <name> --list`, only under a parsed `VIOLA_NAME` and only after its strict-modes check passed, writes `process-start` and `process-exit{subject:"self"}` (`exit_code` 0 with no detail, or `exit_code` 1 `detail:"no-session"` on an empty chain) into the CALLER's `cli-<VIOLA_NAME>.ndjson`, and with no name opens none (chunk 2026-10-17-cli-machine-contract);
 `viola plugin install`, only under a parsed `VIOLA_NAME` and only after its strict-modes check passed, writes `process-start` and `process-exit{subject:"self"}` into the caller's `cli-<VIOLA_NAME>.ndjson`, and with no name opens none; `verify`, once `check_home_tree` has passed over its home, `ledger/`, `bin/` and `plugin/` (a refusal opens no role file and writes no line), writes its `process-start`/`process-exit{subject:"self"}` pair, with eight spawn pairs between them — `version-probe` around the `--version` read, `verify-probe` around the print-mode probe and one `verify-pty-probe` pair around each interactive run (Run A, Run B, Run C, Run D, then Run E) and one `agents-probe` pair around Run B's `claude agents --json` read (no row text, prompt, id or path in any line), each `process-start{subject}` then `process-exit{subject, child_exit_status, duration_ms}` from verify's own call-site wrapper (a child of an interactive PTY run killed at a Ctrl-C or TERM stop closes its pair with `duration_ms` and a `child_exit_status`, the PTY pump's exit code, since portable-pty reports a code for a signalled child, as measured at chunk 2026-10-14-resume-and-compact-ledger-rows by its resume-run stop case; a print-mode or `--version` probe child killed at the stop is not measured; a stopped run writes only the pairs it started, and its self exit reads `exit_code:1, detail:"interrupted"`) (`run_bounded` itself stays unlogged, so `run`'s gate keeps its one `version-probe` pair) — all written only when `VIOLA_NAME` holds a valid name; `list`'s (chunk 2026-10-11-the-board-viola-list), also only when `VIOLA_NAME` holds a valid name and only after its strict-modes scan passed: `process-start`, one `parse-rejected{parser:"state-entry", detail:"symlink-ignored"|"malformed", count}` per nonzero scan count (naming no entry), one `state-recovered` per replayed snapshot, one `parse-rejected{parser:"config-json"}` per bad threshold key, and `process-exit{subject:"self"}`;
 with no name, or on a refused scan, `list` opens no `cli-*.ndjson`; `mcp.ndjson` (chunk 2026-10-17-mcp-server-for-drivers), written by `viola mcp` once its home and `diagnostics/` passed `check_path` (a refusal opens no role file and writes no line): `process-start{subject:"self"}`, the Tokio client's `channel-request` / `channel-response` lines (none for a frame tool whose instance check or server check fails, and a refused instance check writes no line at all), one client-side `send-refused` per refused `send` text, the `list` tool's `agents-probe` pair and the board's `state-recovered` / `parse-rejected` lines (the `config-json` rejections included), and `process-exit` on stdin EOF — none when Claude Code ends it by a signal, as measured live on claude 2.1.287 at that chunk; `hook-<name>.ndjson`: `hook-invoked`, `hook-decision`, `parse-rejected` (a failed server check writes `hook-decision{detail:"server-verify-failed"}` at WARN, on the dialog path after `hook-invoked{corr:null}` and with `corr:null, decision_emitted:false`; a refused or absent instance writes no line on any path, its check (`trusted`) coming before `read_diagnostics_level` and obs init); `hook`'s drift reports go only to the instance's `diagnostics/detail-hook.ndjson`). One line per `write`; dir 0700, files 0600 on Unix; line format owned by obs and fixed by `schemas/diag-line.v1.json`. Content-bearing detail stays in the instance detail files `instances/<ViolaName>/diagnostics/detail-<role>.ndjson` (the instance files, below).
